# Six-pulse thyristor rectifier (firing angle 30 deg) and diode rectifier on a 400 V supply
#
#   SUPPLY (400 V, three phase sources each behind R + L -> commutation overlap)
#     -- thyristor bridge T1..T6 -- DC: smoothing L + 5 ohm load
#     -- diode bridge D1..D6     -- DC: 2000 uF capacitor + 10 ohm load
#
# Drawn in single-phase mode (diodes and thyristors are single-phase parts): the three phase
# sources SUPPLY.a/b/c are 120 deg apart, each behind 5 mohm + 0.1 mH.
# Gate timing: valve k fires alpha degrees after its natural commutation point. With phase a
# voltage = Vm cos(wt), the natural points are -60 (T1, a+), 0 (T2, c-), 60 (T3, b+), 120 (T4, a-),
# 180 (T5, c+) and 240 deg (T6, b-), so each valve gets ref = -(natural point).
# Ideal DC voltage of the thyristor bridge: 1.35 x 400 x cos 30 = 468 V, minus the commutation
# drop (3/pi) w Ls Id.
#
# Elements used: V behind R + L, THY, D, R, L, C.
#
# Generated by circuits/make_drawings.py; open it in the circuit editor (gui.bat) to see the drawing.
#
# EMTSim netlist: six-pulse rectifiers (drawn with the EMTSim circuit editor)
#
# Format: R/L/C from to value | V from to peak angle freq [R] | SW from to closed|open times... | F from to t_apply [t_clear]
# 8 nodes, 21 elements

.tran 0.00002 0.12

V 0 1  326.6 0 50 0.005 0.0001   # SUPPLY.a
V 0 2  326.6 -120 50 0.005 0.0001   # SUPPLY.b
V 0 3  326.6 120 50 0.005 0.0001   # SUPPLY.c
THY 4 1  30 50 ref=-120 width=120 ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # T4
THY 1 5  30 50 ref=60 width=120 ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # T1
D 7 1  ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # D4
D 1 8  ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # D1
THY 4 2  30 50 ref=120 width=120 ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # T6
THY 2 5  30 50 ref=-60 width=120 ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # T3
D 7 2  ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # D6
D 2 8  ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # D3
THY 4 3  30 50 ref=0 width=120 ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # T2
THY 3 5  30 50 ref=-180 width=120 ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # T5
D 7 3  ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # D2
D 3 8  ron=0.001 roff=1000000   # D5
L 5 6  0.005   # LDC
R 6 4  5   # RLOAD
R 4 0  1000000   # REF_T
C 8 7  0.002   # CDC
R 8 7  10   # RDC
R 7 0  1000000   # REF_D

